.TH "EPX\-PRODUCT\-TEMPLATES" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-product\-templates \- read, create, update and delete product templates
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates [flags]
epx product\-templates [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes product templates, the attribute sets shared by products based on them: create makes one, update replaces one, each from \fB\-\-file\fR; delete deletes one.
.PP
Its reads require the product.product_template_read scope. Its writes require the product.product_template_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx product\-templates create"
Create a product template.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the product template in the JSON object of \fB\-\-file\fR (name, attributes) and prints its id.
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the product.product_template_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx product\-templates delete"
Delete a product template.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the product template ID. Emporix deletes only a template that no product and no parent variant is based on: it refuses one in use with 400 Bad Request (exit 1). An unknown ID is no error: Emporix answers as for a deleted template.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the product.product_template_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx product\-templates get"
Show one product template.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads product templates, the attribute sets shared by products based on them. ATTRIBUTES counts the template\(aqs attributes (\fB\-o json\fR prints their definitions).
.PP
Requires the product.product_template_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, ATTRIBUTES, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx product\-templates list"
List product templates.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads product templates, the attribute sets shared by products based on them. ATTRIBUTES counts the template\(aqs attributes (\fB\-o json\fR prints their definitions).
.PP
Requires the product.product_template_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, ATTRIBUTES, VERSION.
.TP
\fB\-\-language <language>\fR
Language of localized table text; a missing translation shows another, labeled (\fB\-o json\fR prints all). Default: \fBen\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx product\-templates update"
Replace a product template.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx product\-templates update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces product template ID with the JSON object of \fB\-\-file\fR, which names its metadata.version: Emporix refuses it as a conflict (exit 5) when the template changed since. Every update makes a new version of the template; the products based on an earlier version keep it until they are updated to the new one. An unknown ID is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Localized text in the body, such as a name, is a map of translations, e.g. \fB{"en": "gram", "de": "Gramm"}\fR, as \fB\-o json\fR of a read prints it, or with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR LANGUAGE a string in that language, e.g. \fB"gram"\fR with \fB\-\-content\-language\fR en.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the product.product_template_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-content\-language <LANGUAGE>\fR
The LANGUAGE of localized text in the body, or * for maps of translations. Default: \fB*\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
